# `config:key:allow`. `localhost` and `127.0.0.1` are two spellings of one machine and two entries in
# an allowlist, which is what makes this a one-word difference between the two configs rather than a
# different target. Written as an absolute URL because that is the one step form that can reach a
# host the config never names (SPEC §5.1) — `TF057` warns about exactly that and is expected here.
#
# The step fails when the run refuses it, and that failure is not the known answer: the answer is
# whether a request ever arrived at `/blocked`, which only the server can say.

test "a step written as an absolute URL to the other spelling of this machine"
  api GET http://localhost:4507/blocked
  expect status equals 200
